      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What is a System in Package?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">A single package that integrates multiple die, passives and interconnect — a subsystem that ships as one component instead of many separate parts on a board.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Which assembly methods can a SiP combine?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Wire bond, flip chip and surface mount, with stacked or side-by-side die and underfill where the build requires it.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can you shield an RF SiP?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes — EMI shielding is available for RF SiP, along with transfer molding and package-level test.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Why build a SiP instead of placing parts on the board?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">To shrink footprint, shorten interconnect for RF performance, cut placements at board assembly, and reduce a board region to a single component to qualify and source.</div>
    </details>
